    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -870,
        -260
      ],
      "size": [
        620,
        310
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "LaMa removes masked text without diffusion denoise or prompts.\n\n1. Load the source image and a separate red/white mask.\n2. grow=4 covers antialiasing, outlines, and shadow; increase it if glyph edges remain.\n3. padding=96 gives LaMa local background context. Keep distant text regions in separate runs: LaMa normalizes each crop to 256x256, so one huge bounding box loses small-detail resolution.\n4. The saved file is the final image; the large preview shows original then final.\n\nRequired model: big-lama.pt in the configured models/inpaint folder."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
